            "description": "Watch Bayern München vs 1. FC Heidenheim highlights and goals from Bundesliga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on May 2, 2026. The Bundesliga fixture on May 2, 2026 , delivered a spectacle of tactical grit and relentless attacking pressure that kept the 75,000 fans in attendance on the edge of their seats until the final whistle. It was a contest where clinical finishing met sheer perseverance, ensuring the drama lasted well beyond the regulated ninety minutes as two sides with vastly different ambitions collided in a memorable encounter. Heidenheim’s Early Blitz Stuns the Allianz Despite Bayern Munich dominating the early ball possession, it was 1. FC Heidenheim who displayed a masterclass in efficiency during the opening half-hour. The visitors broke the deadlock in the 22nd minute when Marnon-Thomas Busch provided a pinpoint delivery for Budu Zivzivadze , who made no mistake with a composed left-footed finish to give the underdogs a shock lead. The goal appeared to rattle the hosts, and before Bayern could find their rhythm, Heidenheim struck again. In the 31st minute, Busch was once again the architect, setting up Eren Dinkci for a simple tap-in that left the home support in a state of disbelief. Bayern Munich attempted to respond through Hiroki Ito , whose ambitious effort from distance whistled just wide of the post. The pressure from the Bavarian giants was constant, but a lack of clinical finishing in the final third seemed destined to haunt them as the first half drew to a close. However, the momentum shifted just before the interval when Leon Goretzka stepped up to a direct free kick in the 44th minute. The midfielder unleashed a spectacular right-footed strike that curled into the back of the net, giving Bayern a vital lifeline and cutting the deficit to 2-1 heading into the dressing rooms. Tactical Overhaul and the Goretzka Double Recognizing the need for a spark, Bayern manager made a daring quadruple substitution at the start of the second half. Joshua Kimmich , Luis Diaz , Michael Olise , and the prolific Harry Kane were all introduced to the fray, signaling a total offensive commitment. The impact was almost immediate as the hosts pinned Heidenheim back into their own box. In the 56th minute, Min-Jae Kim thought he had equalized, only to see his goal-bound effort heroically cleared off the line by the retreating defense. Undeterred, Bayern found their second goal just a minute later. In the 57th minute, Michael Olise began his influential second-half cameo by swinging in a corner that found Leon Goretzka . The German international remained composed to slot home his second of the match with his right foot, bringing the scores level at 2-2. With over half an hour remaining and 75% of the possession, it seemed only a matter of time before the record champions would complete the comeback and take all three points. Stoppage Time Drama and Olise’s Redemption Football rarely follows a predictable script, and Heidenheim proved their resilience in the 76th minute. Against the run of play, Arijon Ibrahimovic —who had been a creative force for the visitors—found Budu Zivzivadze in the area. The forward made no mistake, firing home his second goal of the afternoon to restore Heidenheim 's lead. Bayern threw everything forward in response, with Luis Diaz coming agonizingly close from the edge of the box, but a series of yellow cards for Jonathan Tah and Konrad Laimer highlighted the growing frustration within the home ranks. As the match entered ten minutes of added time, the tension reached a breaking point. Heidenheim 's Jonas Foehrenbach required lengthy medical treatment as the visitors desperately tried to hold onto their narrow advantage. Marnon-Thomas Busch received a late booking for a cynical foul, and it appeared the visitors might survive the onslaught. However, in the 100th minute, Alphonso Davies found space to provide one final cross for Michael Olise . The French winger controlled the ball outside the box and unleashed a stunning right-footed strike that beat the keeper, securing a dramatic 3-3 draw in the dying seconds of a classic Bundesliga encounter.",
